### Day 6/50 — Queries

A database can hold thousands of pieces of data.
But when we need something,
we don't take everything.
We ask for exactly what we need.

That's what a **query** does.

It retrieves the required data,
leaving the rest where it belongs.
Because imagine taking everything just to find one thing.

Messy, right?

Maybe life is a little like that too.

Not everything needs to be taken.
Not every thought needs to be carried.
Not every problem needs to become ours.

Sometimes, taking only what we need
makes things a little easier to handle.

**Because even data becomes messy
when we take more than what we actually need.**
